{"type":"message","id":"48af622f","parentId":"604c7297","timestamp":"2026-05-19T13:04:05.062Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The `/send` endpoint consistently returns a 1101 error (Worker exception) for POST requests. The GET request didn't return anything (empty). The `/api` endpoint returns \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\" which is just the homepage text.\n\nThe send endpoint seems broken from the server side (error 1101 = unhandled exception in the Cloudflare Worker). This is not something I can fix on my end.\n\nLet me try one more thing - maybe the message needs to be sent differently. Let me try with a different content-type or try the raw endpoint.\n\nActually wait, let me check if there's a different endpoint structure. The error being consistently 1101 on POST to /send suggests the endpoint handler itself is crashing.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-efcd80d4-baa2-4c30-9742-f8f0d8b065a6","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try /messages endpoint and /broadcast\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/messages\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"text\":\"heartbeat test\"}'\n\necho \"---\"\n\n# Try /broadcast\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/broadcast\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"message\":\"heartbeat test\",\"threadId\":\"arbitration\"}'"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":21655,"output":331,"cacheRead":112,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":22098,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779195831964,"responseId":"chatcmpl-907ada1c-2cdb-4de4-bd20-effcf742b178"}}
